==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|stifnen}}, equivalent to {{af|en|stiff|-en|id2=inchoative}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɪfən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stiffen.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪfən|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[stiff]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=President signs Violence Against Women Act|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2013/03/07/politics/obama-violence-against-women-act/index.html|date=2013-03-07|passage=Criminal prosecutions of abusers are generally the responsibility of local authorities, but the act '''stiffened''' sentences for stalking under federal law.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Parija Kavilanz|title=This robot makes a T-shirt from start to finish|magazine=w:CNN Business|url=https://money.cnn.com/2016/10/11/technology/robots-garment-manufacturing-sewbo/index.html|date=2016-10-11|passage=It followed a sequence of functions: a machine cuts cloth panels to be sewn, the panels are drenched with the polymer and '''stiffened''', a robotic arm uses suction cups to lift each panel and position it in a sewing machine. Finally, the robotic arm lifts the stitched T-shirt off the sewing machine. {{...}} The system could work for most fabrics, with the exception of leather and waterproof materials that can't be drenched with the '''stiffening''' polymer. {{...}} Zornow has patents pending in 10 countries for the process to '''stiffen''' fabric.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[stiff]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Yoko Ogawa|title=The Housekeeper and the Professor|passage=Bewildered by the unexpected greeting, my son '''stiffened''', but managed a polite answer.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Dr. Melina Jampolis|title=The real science behind fascia ailments|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2018/11/08/health/fascia-blasting-explainer-exercise-jampolis/index.html|date=2018-11-08|passage=He does note that fascia, like most connective tissue in the body, '''stiffens''' with age, overuse and injury.}}

